king comments;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.23(c)(1)(B)","follow, restate, and give complex oral instructions to perform specific tasks, answer questions, or solve problems;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.23(c)(1)(C)","give an organized presentation with a specific point of view;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.23(c)(1)(D)","advocate a position using anecdotes, analogies, and/or illustrations employing eye contact, speaking rate, volume, enunciation, a variety of natural gestures, and conventions of language to communicate ideas effectively;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.23(c)(1)(E)","participate collaboratively in discussions, plan agendas with clear goals and deadlines, set time limits for speakers, take notes, and vote on key issues; and","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.23(c)(1)(F)","develop social communication and produce oral language in contextualized and purposeful ways.","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.23(c)(2)(A)","demonstrate and apply phonetic knowledge; and","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.23(c)(2)(B)","write complete words, thoughts, and answers legibly.","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.23(c)(3)(A)","use print or digital resources to determine the meaning, syllabication, pronunciation, word origin, and part of speech;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.23(c)(3)(B)","use context within or beyond a paragraph to clarify the meaning of unfamiliar or ambiguous words;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.23(c)(3)(C)","determine the meaning and usage of grade-level academic English words derived from Greek, Latin, and other languages, including ast, qui, path, mand/mend, and duc; auto, bio, graph, meter, phon, port, and tele; and terr, chrono, audi, geo, dict, photo, and ject;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.23(c)(3)(D)","identify and use words that name actions, directions, positions, sequences, and locations;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.23(c)(3)(E)","use multiple-meaning words, homographs, homophones, and commonly confused terms correctly; and","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.23(c)(3)(F)","investigate expressions such as idioms and word relationships such as antonyms, synonyms, and analogies.","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.23(c)(4)","Developing and sustaining foundational language skills: listening, speaking, reading, writing, and thinking--fluency. The student reads grade-level text with fluency and comprehension. Based on the student's language proficiency level, the student is expected to adjust fluency when reading grade-level text based on the reading purpose.","strand","4",null],[1,"128.23(c)(5)","Developing and sustaining foundational language skills: listening, speaking, reading, writing, and thinking--self-sustained reading. The student reads grade-appropriate texts independently. Based on the student's language proficiency level, the student is expected to self-select text and read independently for a sustained period of time.","strand","5",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(A)","establish purpose for reading assigned and self-selected texts;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(B)","generate questions about text before, during, and after reading to deepen understanding and gain information;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(C)","make and correct or confirm predictions using text features, characteristics of genre, and structures;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(D)","create mental images to deepen understanding;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(E)","make connections to personal experiences, ideas in other texts, and society;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(F)","make inferences and use evidence to support understanding;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(G)","evaluate details read to determine key ideas;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(H)","synthesize information to create new understanding; and","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(6)(I)","monitor comprehension and make adjustments such as re-reading, using background knowledge, asking questions, and annotating when understanding breaks down.","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(A)","describe personal connections to a variety of sources, including self-selected texts;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(B)","write responses that demonstrate understanding of texts, including comparing sources within and across genres;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(C)","use text evidence to support an appropriate response;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(D)","paraphrase and summarize texts in ways that maintain meaning and logical order;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(E)","interact with sources in meaningful ways such as notetaking, annotating, freewriting, or illustrating;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(F)","respond using newly acquired vocabulary as appropriate;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(G)","discuss and write about the explicit or implicit meanings of text;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(H)","respond orally or in writing with appropriate register, vocabulary, tone, and voice;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(I)","reflect on and adjust responses as new evidence is presented; and","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(7)(J)","defend or challenge the claims using relevant text evidence.","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.23(c)(8)(A)","analyze how themes are developed through the interaction of characters and events;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.23(c)(8)(B)","analyze how characters' motivations and behaviors influence events and resolution of the conflict;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.23(c)(8)(C)","analyze non-linear plot development such as flashbacks, foreshadowing, subplots, and parallel plot structures and compare it to linear plot development; and","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.23(c)(8)(D)","explain how the setting influences the values and beliefs of characters.","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.23(c)(9)(A)","demonstrate knowledge of literary genres such as realistic fiction, adventure stories, historical fiction, mysteries, humor, fantasy, science fiction, and short stories;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.23(c)(9)(B)","identify structural elements such as rhyme, repetition, and alliteration and analyze how language contributes to the meaning of a poem;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.23(c)(9)(C)","analyze the effect of graphical elements such as punctuation and line length in poems across a variety of poetic forms such as epic, lyric, and humorous poetry;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.23(c)(9)(D)","analyze how playwrights develop dramatic action through the use of acts and scenes;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.23(c)(9)(E)","analyze characteristics and structural elements of informational text, including: (i) the controlling idea or thesis with supporting evidence; (ii) features such as footnotes, endnotes, and citations; and (iii) multiple organizational patterns within a text to develop the thesis;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.23(c)(9)(F)","analyze characteristics and structures of argumentative text by: (i) identifying the claim and analyzing the argument; (ii) identifying and explaining the counter argument; and (iii) identifying the intended audience or reader; and","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.23(c)(9)(G)","analyze characteristics of multimodal and digital texts.","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.23(c)(10)(A)","explain the author's purpose and message within a text;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.23(c)(10)(B)","analyze how the use of text structure contributes to the author's purpose;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.23(c)(10)(C)","analyze the author's use of print and graphic features to achieve specific purposes;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.23(c)(10)(D)","describe how the author's use of figurative language such as extended metaphor achieves specific purposes;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.23(c)(10)(E)","identify and analyze the use of literary devices, including multiple points of view and irony;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.23(c)(10)(F)","analyze how the author's use of language contributes to the mood, voice, and tone; and","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.23(c)(10)(G)","explain the purpose of rhetorical devices such as analogy and juxtaposition and of logical fallacies such as bandwagon appeals and circular reasoning.","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.23(c)(11)(A)","plan a first draft by selecting a genre appropriate for a particular topic, purpose, and audience using a range of strategies such as discussion, background reading, and personal interests;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.23(c)(11)(B)","develop drafts into a focused, structured, and coherent piece of writing by: (i) organizing with purposeful structure, including an introduction, transitions, coherence within and across paragraphs, and a conclusion; and (ii) developing an engaging idea reflecting depth of thought with specific facts, details, and examples;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.23(c)(11)(C)","revise drafts for clarity, development, organization, style, word choice, and sentence variety;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.23(c)(11)(D)","edit drafts using standard English conventions, including: (i) complete simple, compound, and complex sentences with subject-verb agreement and avoidance of splices, run-ons, and fragments; (ii) consistent, appropriate use of verb tenses and active and passive voice; (iii) conjunctive adverbs; (iv) prepositions and prepositional phrases and their influence on subject-verb agreement; (v) pronoun-antecedent agreement; (vi) subordinating conjunctions to form complex sentences; (vii) correct capitalization; (viii) punctuation, including commas in nonrestrictive phrases and clauses, semicolons, colons, and parentheses; and (ix) correct spelling, including commonly confused terms such as its/it's, affect/effect, there/their/they're, and to/two/too; and","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.23(c)(11)(E)","publish written work for appropriate audiences.","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.23(c)(12)(A)","compose literary texts such as personal narratives, fiction, and poetry using genre characteristics and craft;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.23(c)(12)(B)","compose informational texts, including multi-paragraph essays that convey information about a topic, using a clear controlling idea or thesis statement and genre characteristics and craft;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.23(c)(12)(C)","compose multi-paragraph argumentative texts using genre characteristics and craft; and","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.23(c)(12)(D)","compose correspondence that reflects an opinion, registers a complaint, or requests information in a business or friendly structure.","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(A)","generate student-selected and teacher-guided questions for formal and informal inquiry;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(B)","develop and revise a plan;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(C)","refine the major research question, if necessary, guided by the answers to a secondary set of questions;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(D)","identify and gather relevant information from a variety of sources;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(E)","differentiate between primary and secondary sources;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(F)","synthesize information from a variety of sources;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(G)","differentiate between paraphrasing and plagiarism when using source materials;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(H)","examine sources for: (i) reliability, credibility, and bias, including omission; and (ii) faulty reasoning such as bandwagon appeals, repetition, and loaded language;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(I)","display academic citations and use source materials ethically; and","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.23(c)(13)(J)","use an appropriate mode of delivery, whether written, oral, or multimodal, to present results.","expectation","13",null]]}